 "notes": [
  "Source: E:\\HaloBaselines\\halo1\\maps\\a10.map (patcher baseline, read-only); plugins E:\\Assembly-1-2023-11-29-1702446457\\Plugins (loose copy of the Assembly Halo1MCC/Halo1 set; the HCEEK kit was not touched).",
  "Legendary = matg Difficulty \"Impossible\" column throughout.",
  "Damage per hit = jpt! Damage Upper Bound mean x jpt! per-material modifier (shield material = coll Shield Material Type; body = the coll material named \"body\") x that coll material's Shield/Body Damage Multiplier. No headshots, no melee, no AOE.",
  "Elite pool = actv Body/Shield Vitality (+0x200/+0x204, the actor-variant override; equal to the coll maxima for the minor) x matg Enemy Vitality / Enemy Shield.",
  "Player times: 30 Hz tick simulation of the measured H1 trigger (rate/30 per tick, shot at sum >= 1, sum resets; rate ramp by the runtime Rate Of Fire Acceleration Rate per tick; plasma heat cools while firing). Halo 1 has no fire-recovery-time field: the rate is the only limit. Flat-rate weapons match ttk_common.player_time (asserted).",
  "Shield recharge: coll Stun Time (+0x10C) is reported as the recharge delay. Its unit is NOT verified in game for H1 (the Elite's 12 vs the cyborg's 6; matg Impossible Enemy Recharge 2.0 is assumed to scale the recharge RATE, not the delay).",
  "AI damage = jpt x matg Enemy Damage x actv Weapon Damage Modifier (+0xC4). The player is NOT scaled by any vitality dial (matg Friend dials apply to allies).",
  "AI \"held\" = the AI firing continuously at its trigger-pull rate; \"paced\" = in its own bursts. Both count every shot as a hit; first-burst delay, aim error and leading are ignored.",
  "Halo 1 has no Brutes."
 ]
